{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1720,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Boiling point is something that we normally think of as a stable property of a substance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5940,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it really depends on what the pressure is around the substance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10000,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so, for example, water only boils at 100 degrees Celsius, if the pressure is 1 atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you reduce the pressure, then those water molecules that are going quite quickly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19520,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can easily escape from the water if there's no pressure pushing down on them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23140,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can get water to boil at room temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25440,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is really boiling water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28500,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The funny thing about boiling water at room temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that it actually decreases the temperature of the water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34480,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because all the fastest water molecules escape,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37120,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving only the slow ones behind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39140,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are refrigerating the water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41880,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Refrigerating the water, by boiling it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43460,
    "dDurationMs": 980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, yes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44440,
    "dDurationMs": 620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(Laughing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45060,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a cool concept."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46540,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know everyone's a big fan of liquid nitrogen, but I've never seen solid nitrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50340,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we used the same trick, pumping out the very fastest nitrogen molecules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53900,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And eventually, that decreased the temperature enough that the nitrogen actually froze."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58580,
    "dDurationMs": 7780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(Laughing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66700,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm putting a thermocouple in there so we can measure the temperature of our liquid nitrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71260,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it reads..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78740,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so the temperature of our liquid nitrogen is about minus 196 Celsius."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82740,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is exactly what it should be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84160,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now we're going to evacuate the chamber."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87100,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna suck the air out of there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90420,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can see that the nitrogen is boiling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96640,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The temperature's dropping, minus 199, minus 200..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're coming up on the triple point of nitrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104900,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're forming solid nitrogen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129580,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ice is actually getting sucked up by the reduced pressure up here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132820,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there is a higher pressure underneath the ice because the vacuum pump hasn't had a chance to work there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138980,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've never seen solid nitrogen before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155980,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After creating the solid nitrogen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we poured it onto a water bath."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160400,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we got the whole surface so cold that carbon dioxide actually condensed out of the atmosphere,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165800,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we formed solid carbon dioxide, dry ice, on the surface of the water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230120,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have a solid piece of CO2"
    } ]
  } ]
}
